294 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(FILE 002 / LETTER FROM PARIS)/Pg 12 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

295 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(A letter from Paris)/Pg 12 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

296 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(I have always believed getting dressed is about more than clothes. A suit can be beautiful, expensive and perfectly tailored\204and still mean very little if the man inside it has handed everyone else the responsibility of telling him who he is. That is why The Blueprint begins with ownership.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

297 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(Guy Ritchie put words around an idea that stayed with me:)/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

298 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(\215if you do not own something, you are not the boss. You have to take full responsibility for what you do. You must become the master of your own kingdom.\216 )/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

299 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(I don't take that to mean a man controls everything that happens to him. He doesn't. It means taking responsibility for what actually belongs to him: his choices, his preparation, his appearance, his word, his response and the work he leaves behind. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

300 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(The world has rules. Menswear certainly has a few. Learn them. There is freedom in knowing what you're doing.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

301 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(And as Ritchie put it:)/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

302 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(\215Hate the player hate the game.\216)/Pg 12 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

303 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(\215Don't hate the game. Love the game. You're in it.\216)/Pg 12 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

304 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(Own the game. Accept the rules. Understand why they exist. Then know them well enough to bend them toward your own narrative without losing your principles. It is your story after all. This guide will show you the navy suit: the shirts, ties, shoes, structure, combinations and occasions.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

305 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(But underneath all of that is one larger idea: Own the suit.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

306 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(Do not wear it because someone told you a grown man should. Don't wear it hoping the label will do your introducing for you. Learn it. Tailor it. Personalize it. Know why each piece is there. Then wear it until it feels like yours.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

307 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 240 0 R/E(Go to the meeting. Take her to dinner. Give the speech. Build the company. Attend the wedding. Sit with your family. Keep your word. Do the work.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

